1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,266
Meet Atlas Office.

2
00:00:01,266 --> 00:00:07,316
One request brings the team together to prepare a Chengdu food and tea product launch.

3
00:00:07,316 --> 00:00:13,506
This is a business simulation using a real model connection and executable local skills.

4
00:00:13,506 --> 00:00:19,766
Atlas chooses the work, assigns colleagues, runs the tools, and creates the deliverables.

5
00:00:20,966 --> 00:00:25,565
The organisation chart connects roles, reporting lines and capacity.

6
00:00:25,565 --> 00:00:34,628
Select a colleague to inspect their manager, available hours and assigned skills: the company context Atlas uses when delegating work.

7
00:00:35,828 --> 00:00:38,971
The people directory makes each role inspectable.

8
00:00:38,971 --> 00:00:48,015
Search Finance to see Deng’s workload, reporting line and executable skills, all attached to the same fictional colleague used in the launch.

9
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:52,765
The library contains sixty-nine executable skills.

10
00:00:52,765 --> 00:00:58,018
Filter by function, search for a capability, and inspect its instructions.

11
00:00:58,018 --> 00:01:03,627
These are the same skill contracts the agent reads and calls during the launch.

12
00:01:04,827 --> 00:01:08,658
Atlas turns the request into a visible execution plan.

13
00:01:08,658 --> 00:01:13,696
Each step has an actual skill, an assigned colleague, and dependencies.

14
00:01:13,696 --> 00:01:17,669
The model reads the skill contracts before it uses them.

15
00:01:17,669 --> 00:01:23,558
The plan and progress come from the running agent, not a prewritten video sequence.

16
00:01:24,758 --> 00:01:26,882
The first results are arriving.

17
00:01:26,882 --> 00:01:33,527
Atlas supplies the skill inputs itself and delegates to colleagues whose profiles allow the work.

18
00:01:33,527 --> 00:01:38,186
Every call is recorded with its assignee, outcome, and elapsed time.

19
00:01:38,186 --> 00:01:41,954
Completed results become context for the next decision.

20
00:01:43,154 --> 00:01:45,772
The agent continues across the company.

21
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:52,887
Planning, responsibilities, capacity and commercial decisions are handled through the same shared runtime.

22
00:01:52,887 --> 00:01:57,451
Dependent steps can proceed only after their prerequisites complete.

23
00:01:57,451 --> 00:02:01,075
There are no manual skill forms between these actions.

24
00:02:02,275 --> 00:02:06,252
The launch takes shape as business records and real files.

25
00:02:06,252 --> 00:02:13,520
Finance calculations, project work, launch risks and management outputs are linked to recorded skill runs.

26
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:21,541
Simulation assumptions remain visible in the content, while the document and spreadsheet generation actually execute.

27
00:02:22,741 --> 00:02:28,492
Atlas brings the completed work into the launch handoff and reusable company knowledge.

28
00:02:28,492 --> 00:02:32,656
The same request drives the workflow through its final outputs.

29
00:02:32,656 --> 00:02:39,332
The live dashboard keeps the completed work, remaining steps, generated files, and API usage visible.

30
00:02:40,532 --> 00:02:48,107
This run recorded 20 completed skill executions, covering 16 different skills and 7 colleagues.

31
00:02:48,107 --> 00:02:49,781
It produced 10 files.

32
00:02:49,781 --> 00:02:54,804
The dashboard also reports 24 model requests and 26 tool calls.

33
00:02:54,804 --> 00:03:00,783
These are measured results from this run, not projected productivity gains.

34
00:03:01,983 --> 00:03:05,188
Every completed step links to its actual result.

35
00:03:05,188 --> 00:03:12,398
The activity record keeps the inputs and outputs, while the file library contains the generated launch pack.

36
00:03:12,398 --> 00:03:18,139
You can reopen the conversation later and inspect the same persisted execution record.

37
00:03:19,339 --> 00:03:27,971
Open the recorded proposal to examine the approach: a fifty-thousand-renminbi pilot versus a hundred-and-twenty-thousand full launch.

38
00:03:27,971 --> 00:03:33,876
The actual result includes the recommendation, weighted scores and editable proposal files.

39
00:03:35,076 --> 00:03:40,096
Activity brings together all twenty recorded runs and their company records.

40
00:03:40,096 --> 00:03:44,192
Each result retains its inputs, output and assigned colleague.

41
00:03:44,192 --> 00:03:49,278
The review counter clearly distinguishes pending actions from completed work.

42
00:03:50,478 --> 00:03:53,964
The file library gathers the launch pack in one place.

43
00:03:53,964 --> 00:04:02,550
Search company knowledge to retrieve the saved launch note, carrying the decision, assumptions and evidence forward into future work.

44
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:08,344
Settings expose tourism proposal modes and delivery permissions.

45
00:04:08,344 --> 00:04:14,516
Connections lists optional Google, Telegram and MCP services with their actual status.

46
00:04:14,516 --> 00:04:18,822
The API reference documents the same skills for integration.

47
00:04:20,022 --> 00:04:29,334
Atlas Office makes agent work inspectable: one brief, a delegated plan, executable skills, and a finished set of business outputs.

48
00:04:29,334 --> 00:04:38,360
The GitHub repository includes the application, sixty-nine skill contracts, the API reference, and the evidence from this run.

49
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:44,807
The business launch is simulated; the agent execution and generated deliverables are real.
